        }
      ],
      "words": 75
    },
    {
      "block": "原句13",
      "no": 13,
      "segments": [
        {
          "text": "“I forgot how pretty it gets.”",
          "ok": true,
          "pos": 22608
        },
        {
          "text": "I looked at Willow Creek through her eyes. Not mine. Not as the place that kept celebrating after Pops died. Not as the ",
          "ok": true,
          "pos": 22657
        },
        {
          "text": "Maybe that was what scared me most. Somewhere along the last five years, I had convinced myself I didn’t need any of it",
          "ok": true,
          "pos": 22971
        },
        {
          "text": "Tonight was the first time I wondered if that had ever been true",
          "ok": true,
          "pos": 23091
        }
      ],
